# 🚗 Smart Parking System

An IoT-based **Smart Parking System** that automates vehicle entry using **ESP32, RFID, ultrasonic sensing, servo motor, MySQL, and a Flask web dashboard**.

The project demonstrates how embedded systems, sensors, databases, and web technologies can be integrated to build a real-world parking automation system.

---

## 📌 Project Overview

Traditional parking systems often depend on manual verification and monitoring.

The goal of this project is to explore:

> **How can vehicle entry be automatically authorized, recorded, and monitored through an IoT-based system?**

The system combines:

- ESP32 for hardware control
- RC522 RFID for vehicle/user identification
- Servo motor for automatic gate control
- Ultrasonic sensor for detecting vehicle movement at the entry gate
- MySQL for storing vehicle, parking, and access information
- Flask for the web dashboard
- HTML, CSS, and JavaScript for the dashboard interface

The current implementation focuses on **vehicle entry management**. Exit processing is intentionally not implemented.

---

## 🎯 Objectives

The main objectives of this project are:

- Automate vehicle entry using RFID
- Verify registered RFID users
- Control the parking gate automatically
- Record successful vehicle entries
- Store vehicle and owner information
- Maintain parking session status
- Record authorized and denied RFID access attempts
- Monitor parking information through a web dashboard
- Display the number of vehicles and access activity

---

## ✨ Features

### 🔐 RFID-Based Vehicle Identification

The RC522 RFID reader scans the RFID card.

The ESP32 checks the RFID UID against registered users stored in MySQL.

The system verifies:

- RFID UID
- User status
- Owner name
- Vehicle number

Only registered and active RFID cards are allowed to enter.

---

### 🚦 RFID Access Control

The system provides two access results:

```text
ALLOWED
DENIED
